From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0403-black-world-04-upscale-trace-by-sizes.patch

Source: 0403-black-world-04-upscale-trace-by-sizes.patch
(catches a world that comes and goes)

Run75 (Docked) showed a live world only in its last ~35 s, right after eight new compute
pipelines (414-433 s) and unbacked 2560x1440 render targets (435 s); run79 (Handheld) showed one
near 440 s, where the texture cache made 1,888 then 4,127 images in 600 frames and frames ran to
684 ms. Neither has an upscale line near the flip: the per-program lines log once, and the trace
had no lines left. The likeliest flip is the game's own resolution path: under such a load the 3D
size drops, the network (1:1 at Max Resolution) becomes an upscale, the stand-in finds a pair the
usual way and the world shows; back at 1:1 there is no pair and the frame is black again.

The trace texts now carry sizes and formats only (addresses rotate every frame and would use the
lines up), 64 lines per program, so a change of the network's input size is one line each way:
"program handles: 1600x900 format 32 -> 1920x1080 format 33, blitted" against "no pair (...):
r@0xc0 1920x1080 format 32 ... w@0xd0 1920x1080 format 33". The once-per-program handle inventory
keeps the addresses. Default behaviour unchanged. Clang syntax check, no warnings; not built, not
run.

